    "https://www.apsu.edu/human-resources/hiring/faculty.php": {
      "title": "Request to Fill Position",
      "description": "Faculty Recruitment and Hiring Process Overview Toggle Menu Toggle Search Go back Alumni Current Students Faculty & Staff Military Parents & Families Close Search Submit Close Search A-Z Index People Search Apply Request Info Visit Give Calendar About APSU Admissions Academics Campus Life Athletics I Am... Alumni Current Student Faculty/Staff Military Parent/Family Apply Request Info Visit Give Calendar Home » Human Resources » Recruitment, Hiring, & Onboarding » Faculty Recruiting & Hiring Process Faculty Recruiting & Hiring Process As a hiring manager, you play a critical role in the selection and retention of Austin\n                     Peay State University’s workforce. Selecting the right candidate for a job opening\n                     is one of your most important functions as a manager. We hope this page will serve as a tool and a reference for you as a hiring manager\n                     at Austin Peay State University. Faculty Search Committee Training Search Committee Confidentiality Agreement Request to Fill Position The first step to filling a vacant position is the Department Chair initiates a new\n                     requisition. During this process, the job description will be reviewed to ensure it\n                     accurately reflects the position, advertising sources are identified, and search committees\n                     are formed. It is then routed forward for all appropriate approvals. The average time for the request to recieve all approvals is 7 days. Govs Suite Training Materials Posting Once the request to fill is approved by all parties, it will be posted on the Austin\n                     Peay website for a minimum of 30 calendar days . Human Resources will place an ad in HigherEdJobs and The Chronicle of Higher Ed.\n                     Human Resources will advertise in additional locations should the hiring department\n                     wish to do so, however the hiring departments are responsible for the cost of the\n                     advertisement. Review Applications Applications will be available to Department Chair immediately upon submission. Once\n                     the Department Chair/search committee selects candidates for interviews, move candidates\n                     to the appropriate phase (example: Selected for Initial Interview). The department\n                     will notify, schedule, and perform the interviews. References should be contacted after final interviews have been scheduled. Hiring Proposal Once interviews have been conducted and a candidate has been recommended for hire\n                     by the search committee/department, the Search Committee Chair will change the status\n                     of the candidate to Recommend for Hire (OIC Review) in Govs Suite. The Department Chair will receive notification once OIC approves. Then they will extend\n                     the verbal offer. After the candidate accepts the position, the Hiring Manager will then start the Hiring\n                        Proposal process in Govs Suite. Govs Suite Training Materials Make An Offer Once the Office of Institutional Culture has reviewed the candidate and interview\n                        documents, the Department Chair will make the offer to the candidate, indicate the\n                        accepted salary and start date, and move the workflow to Human Resources. HR will\n                        generate an employment agreement that will be sent to the employee via Govs Suite. Employment Agreements will not be generated by the Office of Human Resources if a\n                           candidate is deemed not qualified for an advertised position. Notify Applicants After receiving the signed contract, HR will mark the posting as filled, which automatically\n                        sends rejection emails to all unsuccessful applicants. Before doing this, HR will\n                        ask the Department Chair to personally email any candidates who reached the interview\n                        stage. Providing a direct, personalized rejection is important because it offers closure\n                        and acknowledges the time and effort those candidates invested. Office of Human Resources Hours : Monday to Friday 8:00am to 4:30pm Location : Browning Room 002 PO Box 4507 Contact Information : Phone: (931) 221-7177 Fax: (931) 221-6345 hr@apsu.edu Austin Peay State University 601 College Street Clarksville, TN 37044 (931) 221-7011 Clarksville Campus Austin Peay Center at Fort Campbell Felix G. Woodward Library Home OneStop Pathway Careers at APSU Non-Discrimination Policy Title IX ADA Emergency Management Accreditation Privacy Contact Us Copyright © 2026 Facebook Youtube Twitter Instagram ©"
    },
    "https://www.apsu.edu/human-resources/index.php": {
      "title": "Office of Human Resources",
      "description": "APSU Human Resources | Employment, Benefits & Career Opportunities Austin Peay State University Toggle Menu Toggle Search Go back Alumni Current Students Faculty & Staff Military Parents & Families Close Search Submit Close Search A-Z Index People Search Apply Request Info Visit Give Calendar About APSU Admissions Academics Campus Life Athletics I Am... Alumni Current Student Faculty/Staff Military Parent/Family Apply Request Info Visit Give Calendar Your browser does not support the video tag. Office of Human Resources × Cultivating a Community of Excellence and Support At Austin Peay State University, our dedicated faculty and staff are the foundation of our success. The Office of Human Resources is committed to fostering a vibrant and supportive environment where every employee can excel and feel valued. We provide comprehensive services and strategic guidance to support you throughout your entire journey at APSU—from the day you apply to the day you retire. Explore the resources here to manage your benefits, discover professional development opportunities, and find the information you need to thrive as a Gov. Join Our Team Find your next career at the region's university of choice. Search our open positions to see how you can contribute to our vibrant campus community. Apply Now! Commitment to Hiring Veterans Total Compensation Calculator Employee Salary Database New Employee Onboarding Explore Human Resources Benefits & Wellness Your health and well-being are a top priority. Explore the comprehensive insurance, retirement, and wellness programs available to you and your family as an APSU employee. Events Calendar Stay up to date with important events and opportunities by regularly checking the HR Events Calendar. Discover upcoming workshops, training sessions, and activities designed to support your professional development and engagement. Holidays Find the official university holiday schedule for the calendar year. See a complete list of dates when the university will be closed for holiday observances. Govs Suite Hiring Access the university's integrated talent management system. This portal is your home for viewing and applying for open positions at APSU. Performance Evaluations Access resources for the annual performance evaluation process for both employees and managers. Find guides, forms, and timelines to facilitate a productive and meaningful review. Retirement Planning Prepare for your future with our retirement planning resources. Learn about the mandatory and voluntary retirement plans offered to APSU employees. Quick Links Be Fit. Be Well. Be A Gov. Classification and Compensation Study Employment Verification Essential Employees Hiring Process HR Forms Immigration Learn. Grow. Lead Notice of Availability of Form 1095-C Upon Request Effective for the 2025 tax year , employees who wish to receive a copy of their Form 1095- may request one using the instructions below. How to Request Your Form: If you would like to receive a copy of your Form 1095-C (or 1095-B) , you may submit a by emailing humanresources@apsu.edu . Upon receiving your request, we will provide your form within 30 days . Electronic Delivery Option: If you are a current employee and prefer to receive your form electronically, you must provide consent. To opt-in for electronic delivery, please follow these instructions . You may withdraw your consent at any time using the same method. For any questions regarding your Form 1095-C, please contact Human Resources. TAKE THE NEXT STEPS Office of Institutional Culture Finance & Administration Payroll Office of Human Resources Monday - Friday: 8:00 a.m. - 4:30 p.m. About Us Frequently Asked Questions APSU Policies Contact Us Human Resources Browning Building Room 002 PO Box 4507 Clarksville, TN 37044 (931) 221-7177 EMAIL US Austin Peay State University 601 College Street Clarksville, TN 37044 (931) 221-7011 Clarksville Campus Austin Peay Center at Fort Campbell Felix G. Woodward Library Home OneStop Pathway Careers at APSU Non-Discrimination Policy Title IX ADA Emergency Management Accreditation Privacy Contact Us Copyright © 2026 Facebook Youtube Twitter Instagram ©"
